## Session 6 summary

**Criteria status: NOT met — marker not written.** But this session converted a 100%-fail catastrophic state into a single remaining transient plus a pace shortfall.

**Five root causes proven and fixed this session (all RULE-4 instrumented chains):**

1. **FIX-11** — the acquire-reload deferred-stale honor point (`P5-DEFERRED-STALE`) invalidated buffers carrying committed-but-undestaged dirents in the post-CIL window (proven run81 r5: node8's 46 md5 adds destroyed at 157.307, platter kept the peer's older image cluster-wide). Undestaged guard added at the honor point and both reload-walk arms.
2. **FIX-12/12b** — the no-inode BAST release violated Invariant-1: its single-AG drain missed cross-AG dir blocks (dir blocks are allocated in each *writer's* AG), and it fires for live-but-IRECLAIMABLE inodes (drop_caches windows). Replaced with an LSN-targeted whole-AIL bounded fence (`xfs_ail_push_upto_sync_bounded`) + a per-mount drained-LSN marker so the hundreds of noino releases per round share one drain; never unlocks undrained (shutdown policy like P3B).
3. **FIX-13** — the phantom-EX (noino release can't demote `i_dlm_mode`) defeated the P116 self-clobber guard: a dead inode incarnation was kept as "authoritative", and `dd`'s O_TRUNC double-freed its stale extent map → defer corruption 0x8 → node shutdown every run (proven run84 test3 @186.65). P116 now verifies the hold against the DLM table (`mxfs_v5_dlm_inode_held_rawmode`).
4. **FIX-14** — the md5-tail cluster-wide loss root: the acquire-fence evict (`P-DE-BLK`) used `(!in_ail || !undestaged)` — CIL-window buffers bypassed the check and were evicted; the re-read DMA'd the platter over committed adds (proven run87 r2 via new bp/lseq/wseq prints). Undestaged check made unconditional at 3 sites. **Result: peers went from all-fail to zero fail rounds.**
5. **FIX-15/15b** — rank1's transient stale readdir: discovered `xfs_buf_incore(flags=0)` blocking-locks in this kernel, so the reload walk's trylock was a *self*-trylock (dead code — everything deferred to the flag path that races the first readdir). Reload now decides inline under the held lock; the honor point got a bounded 50ms wait. Improved but not eliminated (P5D=39 on test1, fail rounds 6-7).

**Remaining blockers (next session):** (a) rank1's stale-serve persists past the 50ms honor-wait — P5D prints now name the busy state to extend the chase; (b) 24 rounds need ~460s vs the 480s budget with test1's fail-path overhead — pace tuning (P60's per-hit FUA compare is a known cost); (c) the once-per-run late-round dir-visibility event (peers can't stat the dir; didn't recur in run89) — needs a capture when it next fires. All evidence paths, build IDs (current: `36600ADF`), and the full fix ledger are in ccmemory `sess6-FIX11-12-13-noino-invariant1-phantom-P116` and `sess6-FIX14-15-cil-window-evict-and-rank1-stale-serve`. run89 artifacts are in the scratchpad (`run89/`) and cluster state is live on build `36600ADF` for the next session to continue the ladder toward 24-round passes, then the full 1/2/4/8 matrix.

